n torrent  server which  actually is where all the data is stored  the torrent suite software helps you  plan your entire run  right from the beginning of of labeling  your samples and  assigning the barcodes and planning your  runs and all the primary data is stored  and analyzed here  where the electrical signals the raw  signals are converted to base calls  and the alignment and base alignments  are are made  once all of this is done then the  variant caller plug-in is used and the  coverage plugin is used  they make the call for the presence or  absence of the variant  and all that data is further analyzed  and summarized for you using the  aggressive  sum toolkit and it provides you  actionable genotypes  so this entire need of of trying to go  back and look at raw data is taken away  because  the agri-sum toolkit really summarizes  everything for you  and gives you the actionable genotypes  in a format  that you can use  so the interpretation what does the  agri-sum toolkit do  and how it makes the results really uh  easy  is that it it summarizes the entire run  for you  showing you what types of markers were  involved in the panel  where their snips deletions insertions  how many amplicons were there  and what's the mean coverage and the  call rate it gives you  the marker performance and it can be  categorized into  any into several bins as per your  requirement  and similarly for the sample call rates  and we use the simple traffic signal  like green being good  yellow or oranges be watchful and  red is that things have failed go check  out what has happened  the agmvsum toolkit also presents this  data  into very easy interpretable format  in in bar graph so on this bar graph on  the  y-axis you have the number of samples  and  on the x-axis you have the call rate  range  and then you look at a graph like this  where you are seeing  green bars which is good and wherever  you are seeing red bars that means it is  bad and these samples have failed or  need 